  "task": {
    "objective": "Deliver two supplies for each polity while scouting, paying finite signal costs, interpreting expiring warnings, and committing caravans to safe-stop road segments.",
    "natural_termination": "Success when all three delivery counts reach two. Failure when any polity's bank plus caravan cargo plus already delivered supplies falls below two, making its required delivery impossible.",
    "interaction": "Tending a tower spends shared finite fuel to give peers a dated, finite-lived hazard snapshot. Their later segment commitments encounter actual moving hazards and shared road occupancy; a blocked caravan can lose cargo while waiting, while alternative lanes cost extra scout/driver time.",
    "observation_access": "Partially observable. Static map, safe stops, destinations, towers/fuel, delivery totals, signal flags and phase are public. Scouts have radii 3,3,4. A role also sees hazards within one of its own caravan and always knows its own caravan/home; other scouts, caravans and homes require scout sight. Invisible fields are -1 with explicit masks. Warning entities show only their recipient's stored snapshot, direction, timestamp and remaining lifetime. A live warning never reveals the actual hazard's current state; actual hazard entity visibility remains local. Per-role blocked/loss flags are private observation fields and are not public scene events."
  },
